<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  BigFix Task Export

  Title    : BigFix Platform Health Check  Run FillDB Performance Log Analyzer (4.0.1)
  ID       : 27399
  Author   : dmccalla
  Domain   : BES
  Imported : 2025-11-21T12:10:00
  Source   : bigfixm1_main @ BES-Root
-->
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>BigFix Platform Health Check -- Run FillDB Performance Log Analyzer (4.0.1)</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[
<STYLE> 				.header { 					font-size: 14px; 					background-color: #990000; 					color: white; 					padding: 6px 40px 6px 10px; 					white-space: nowrap; 				} 				.row { 					font-size: 14px; 					padding: 6px 40px 6px 10px; 					border: 1px solid black; 					border-top: none; 				} 				.nowrap { 					white-space: nowrap; 				} 			</STYLE>

<DIV id=seed_2 style="BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: #1976d2 10px solid; BORDER-BOTTOM: #1976d2 10px solid; BORDER-LEFT: #1976d2 10px solid">
<DIV style="COLOR: white; PADDING-BOTTOM: 10px; PADDING-TOP: 10px; PADDING-LEFT: 10px; PADDING-RIGHT: 10px; BACKGROUND-COLOR: #1976d2"><IMG style="VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0px; PADDING-TOP: 0px; PADDING-LEFT: 0px; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px" src=" data:image/png;base64,"></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 18px; FONT-FAMILY: sans-serif; PADDING-BOTTOM: 20px; PADDING-TOP: 20px; PADDING-LEFT: 20px; PADDING-RIGHT: 20px">
<DIV><STRONG><FONT size=3>Description</FONT></STRONG></DIV><BR>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px">
<P><FONT size=2>This task is for automating portions of a standard BigFix platform health check.&nbsp; Specifically, this task will perform the following steps: </FONT></P>
<UL>
<LI><FONT size=2>Backup any existing perfmon log analyzer results. </FONT>
<LI><FONT size=2>Create the&nbsp;BigFix Platform&nbsp;Health Check&nbsp;folder structure to support running the&nbsp;perfmon analyzer&nbsp;on the same drive that the BigFix&nbsp;client is installed to (configurable in the actionscript). </FONT>
<LI><FONT size=2>Run the analyzer against the log file specfied in the user input fields below.&nbsp; You can enter in a custom file path&nbsp;or use&nbsp;the default location, which is pre-populated.<STRONG>&nbsp;</STRONG> The filename is self explanatory.</FONT>
<UL>
<LI><STRONG><FONT size=2>If log rotation produced multiple log files, which is normal, place them all in the folder specified and the task will automatically combine the log files into a single log for analysis.</FONT></STRONG></LI></UL>
<LI><FONT size=2>The analyzer&nbsp;output will be a .csv file by default, but it is possible to export as table or json by selecting an option in the dropdown below.&nbsp; </FONT></LI></UL></DIV>
<DIV><STRONG><FONT size=3>Deployment Notes</FONT></STRONG></DIV><BR><FONT size=2>
<UL>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>This task can only be run my Master Operators.</FONT></DIV>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>This will only be relevant on BigFix root servers.</FONT></DIV>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Make sure the file that is being analyzed is not a live log file or the&nbsp;analyzer cannot access it.</FONT></DIV>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Run it as a one time action only</FONT>.</DIV>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>The FillDB Performance log analyzer is currently hosted at <A href="https://bigfix-mark.github.io/Tools/MXToolkit.zip">https://bigfix-mark.github.io/Tools/MXToolkit.zip</A></FONT></FONT><FONT size=2>.&nbsp;This task will download and unzip this file in order to&nbsp;access the FillDB Performance analyzer executable. If the download fails it might be due to network restrictions.&nbsp; For AirGap installations, manually download and then&nbsp;copy the file into the ".\BES Server\wwwrootbes\bfmirror\downloads\sha1" folder&nbsp;on your root server. </FONT></DIV></LI>
<UL>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Download failures can also happen when the tools are updated.&nbsp; You will have to update the prefetch statement file size and file hashes&nbsp;to work with the updated file.</FONT></DIV></LI></UL>
<LI>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Depending on the total size of the log file(s), this process may take a few minutes. A typical 1 GB total file size across 10 files takes about 5 minutes. The logs must first be combined and then analyzed.</FONT></DIV></LI></UL>
<DIV><STRONG><FONT size=3>User Input and Parameters</FONT></STRONG></DIV><BR>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>If you need to analyze a log file&nbsp;that is not using the default location (C:\BigFix_Health_Check\Platform\Results\Logs\FillDB_Performance) or default file name (FillDBperf.log) and/or&nbsp;need to change the output from the default of&nbsp;CSV, update the fields below.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px">&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>FillDB Performance Log File Location:</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><BR><INPUT id=filldbPerfFilePath size=80 value=C:\BigFix_Health_Check\Platform\Results\Logs\FillDB_Performance><BR></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Base FillDB Performance Log File Name</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2><EM><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> File</EM> <EM>must have a .log extension. If there are&nbsp;</EM><EM>multiple log files they&nbsp;</EM><EM>should have the default log rotation extension format&nbsp;like .log_1:</EM></FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><BR><INPUT id=filldbPerfFileName value=FillDBperf.log></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><BR><LABEL for=filldbPerfOutputType><FONT size=2>Choose the FillDB performance log output type:</FONT></LABEL></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><LABEL for=filldbPerfOutputType><FONT size=2></FONT></LABEL>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2></FONT><SELECT id=filldbPerfOutputType> <OPTION selected value=csv>CSV</OPTION> <OPTION value=json>JSON</OPTION> <OPTION value=table>Table</OPTION></SELECT><FONT size=2> <BR></FONT><BR><script>document.body.ontakeaction = function(event) {
    if (event.contentID == 'Action1') {

        if (EvaluateRelevance('master flag of current console user') === "False") {
            alert('<?jxlat Only Master Operators can run this Task.?>');
            return false;
        } else {
            var thefilldbPerfFilePath = document.getElementById("filldbPerfFilePath").value;
            var thefilldbPerfFileName = document.getElementById("filldbPerfFileName").value;
            var thefilldbPerfOutputType = document.getElementById("filldbPerfOutputType").value;
            var rootServerWindows = EvaluateRelevance(
                'exists bes computer whose (root server flag of it = true AND operating system of it starts with "Win")'
            );
        }

        if (EvaluateRelevance('master flag of current console user') === 'false') {
            alert("Only Master Operators can run this Task.");
            return false;
        } else

        if (rootServerWindows === 'false') {
            alert("This task can only be run on Windows-based BigFix root servers");
            return false;
        } else

        if (thefilldbPerfFilePath == null || thefilldbPerfFilePath == "") {
            alert("FillDB performance log path field must not be blank.");
            return false;
        } else

        var path = thefilldbPerfFilePath.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, "");   // IE-safe trim

        var validPath = /^[A-Za-z]:\\[^<>:"|?*]+$/.test(path);

        var path = thefilldbPerfFilePath.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, "");

         if (!/^[A-Za-z]:\\[^<>:"|?*]+(\\[^<>:"|?*]+)*$/.test(path)) {
             alert("Please enter a valid Windows directory path for the FillDB performance log path. Example: D:\\Logs\\FillDBPerf");
         return false;
         } else

        if (thefilldbPerfFileName == null || thefilldbPerfFileName == "") {
            alert("FillDB performance log name field must not be blank.");
            return false;
        } else

        var cleanedName = thefilldbPerfFileName.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, ""); // IE-safe trim

        if (!/\.log$/i.test(cleanedName)) {
             alert("FillDB performance log name must end with .log");
             return false;
        } else {

            TakeSecureFixletAction(
                Relevance('id of current fixlet'),
                Relevance('id of current bes site'),
                "Action1",
                {},
                {
                    filldbPerfFilePath: thefilldbPerfFilePath,
                    filldbPerfFileName: thefilldbPerfFileName,
                    filldbPerfOutputType: thefilldbPerfOutputType
                }
            );
        }

        return false;
    }
};</script><BR></DIV>
<DIV><STRONG><FONT size=3>Supported Platforms</FONT></STRONG></DIV><BR>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>Windows</FONT></DIV><BR>
<DIV><STRONG><FONT size=3>Version and Release Notes</FONT></STRONG></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>4.0.1 - Added a&nbsp;note about "stitching" up multiple FillDB performance logs into a single log.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>4.0 - Version sync.&nbsp; Updated prefetch to reflect new version of MXToolkit.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>3.0.0 - Added MO restriction. Version sync with other HC content.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>2.0.0 - Re-branded.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT size=2>1.0.0 - Initial version.</FONT></DIV></DIV></DIV>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>/* IS A WINDOWS ROOT SERVER */ (exists main gather service and not exists relay service) AND (windows of operating system)</Relevance>
    <Category>BigFix Platform Health Check</Category>
    <Source>HCL BigFix AVP and Professional Services</Source>
    <SourceID>Experimental</SourceID>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2025-10-18</SourceReleaseDate>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Fri, 21 Nov 2025 20:09:13 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BES </Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to deploy this action.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[

// ====================================================================================================
//     DESCRIPTION AND NOTES
//
//     - This task will execute the filldb perflog analyzer tool against BigFix perflog files.
// ====================================================================================================


// ====================================================================================================
//     SET SOME PARAMETERS
//
//     - Only "driveLetter" should generally be edited.
//     - Avoid hardcoding any other paths.
// ====================================================================================================

parameter "driveLetter"="{name of drive of regapp "BESClient.exe"}"
parameter "checkType"="Platform"
parameter "rootFolder"="{parameter "driveLetter" & "\BigFix_Health_Check\" & parameter "checkType"}"
parameter "resultsFolder"="{parameter "rootFolder" & "\Results"}"
parameter "toolsFolder"="{parameter "rootFolder" & "\Tools"}"
parameter "backupsFolder"="{parameter "rootFolder" & "\Backup"}"
parameter "scriptsFolder"="{parameter "rootFolder" & "\Scripts"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFolder"="{parameter "filldbPerfFilePath" of action}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsName"="{parameter "filldbPerfFileName" of action}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullName"="{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFolder" & "\" & parameter "fillDBPerfLogsName"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullNameCombined"="{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullName" & "_combined"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder"="{parameter "toolsFolder" & "\FillDB_Performance"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder"="{parameter "scriptsFolder" & "\FillDB_Performance"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"="{parameter "resultsFolder" & "\FillDB_Performance\Analysis"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisName"="{"FillDB_Perf_Analysis_" & computer name & "_" & (((month of it as two digits & "-" & day_of_month of it as two digits & "-" & year of it as string) of date(local time zone) of it & "_" & (two digit hour of it as string & two digit minute of it as string) of time (local time zone) of it) of now) & "." & parameter "filldbPerfOutputType" of action}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFullName"="{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder" & "\" & parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisName"}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsBackupFolder"="{parameter "backupsFolder" & "\Results\FillDB_Performance\Logs\" & (((month of it as two digits & "-" & day_of_month of it as two digits & "-" & year of it as string) of date(local time zone) of it & "_" & (two digit hour of it as string & two digit minute of it as string) of time (local time zone) of it) of now)}"
parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisBackupFolder"="{parameter "backupsFolder" & "\Results\FillDB_Performance\Analysis\"  & (((month of it as two digits & "-" & day_of_month of it as two digits & "-" & year of it as string) of date(local time zone) of it & "_" & (two digit hour of it as string & two digit minute of it as string) of time (local time zone) of it) of now)}"


// ====================================================================================================
//     BACKUP EXISTING ANALYSIS FILES
// ====================================================================================================

if {exists folder (parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder")}
waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisBackupFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C xcopy "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"}" "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisBackupFolder"}"
endif


// ====================================================================================================
//     CLEAN OUT OLD FOLDER STRUCTURES
// ====================================================================================================

waithidden cmd.exe /C rd /s /q "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C rd /s /q "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C rd /s /q "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"}"


// ====================================================================================================
//     REBUILD FOLDER STRUCTURE
// ====================================================================================================

waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "rootFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "toolsFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder"}"
waithidden cmd.exe /C mkdir "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder"}"


// ====================================================================================================
//     DOWNLOAD & STAGE TOOLS
// ====================================================================================================

prefetch unzip-5.52.exe sha1:84debf12767785cd9b43811022407de7413beb6f size:204800 http://software.bigfix.com/download/redist/unzip-6.0.exe sha256:2122557d350fd1c59fb0ef32125330bde673e9331eb9371b454c2ad2d82091ac
prefetch MXToolkit.zip sha1:797022f47e4c5b7578d33edbc454efdf42456508 size:14284048 https://bigfix-mark.github.io/Tools/MXToolkit.zip sha256:26d08928c7e7100d9c64cba5a095a96d347993066e6139b9d5cd30c551a078c1
move "{(pathname of client folder of current site) & "\__Download\MXToolkit.zip"}" "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\MXToolkit.zip"}"
move "{(pathname of client folder of current site) & "\__Download\unzip-5.52.exe"}" "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\unzip-5.52.exe"}"
waithidden "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\unzip-5.52.exe"}" -o "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\MXToolkit.zip"}" -d "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder"}"

// ====================================================================================================
//     CREATE & RUN SCRIPTS
// ====================================================================================================

if {exists file (parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullName")}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//     MULTIPLE LOG FILES - COMBINE AND ANALYZE
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    if {exists files whose (name of it contains "1") of folder (parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFolder")}

		waithidden cmd.exe /C echo Multiple files found..  > "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder" & "\" & (((month of it as two digits & "-" & day_of_month of it as two digits & "-" & year of it as string) of date(local time zone) of it & "_" & (two digit hour of it as string & two digit minute of it as string) of time (local time zone) of it) of now) & "_Analyzer_Log.txt"}"

        // --- Create combine script ---
        delete __createfile
        delete bfCombineFiles.bat
        delete "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfCombineFiles.bat"}"

        createfile until _END_
@echo off
setlocal enabledelayedexpansion

set "inputFolder={parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFolder"}"
set "outputFile={parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullNameCombined"}"

cd /d "%inputFolder%"

if exist "%outputFile%" del "%outputFile%"

:: Build a list of sorted files by numeric name
for /f "tokens=* delims=" %%F in ('dir /b /a:-d ^| sort') do (
    echo Adding %%F
    type "%%F" >> "%outputFile%"
    echo. >> "%outputFile%"
)

endlocal
_END_

        move __createfile "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfCombineFiles.bat"}"

        // Run combine script
        waithidden cmd.exe /C "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfCombineFiles.bat"}"

        // Create analyzer script (combined)
        delete __createfile
        delete bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat

        createfile until _END_
cd "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"}"
"{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\MXFillDBPerf.exe"}" --input "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullNameCombined"}" --format "{parameter "filldbPerfOutputType" of action}" --stats --healthcheck > "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFullName"}"
_END_

        move __createfile "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat"}"

        // Run analyzer script (combined)
        waithidden cmd.exe /C "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat"}"

    else

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//     SINGLE LOG FILE - ANALYZE
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        delete __createfile
        delete bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat

        createfile until _END_
cd "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder"}"
"{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisToolsFolder" & "\MXFillDBPerf.exe"}" --input "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullName"}" --format "{parameter "filldbPerfOutputType" of action}" --stats --healthcheck > "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFullName"}"
_END_

        move __createfile "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat"}"

        waithidden cmd.exe /C "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisScriptsFolder" & "\bfRunFillDBPerfLogAnalyzer.bat"}"

    endif

else

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//     NO LOG FILE FOUND
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    waithidden cmd.exe /C echo Exit Code 1 --> No matching FillDB performance log was present. The file was "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsFullName"}". > "{parameter "fillDBPerfLogsAnalysisFolder" & "\_ANALYZER_ERROR_1.txt"}"

endif]]></ActionScript>
    </DefaultAction>
  </Task>
</BES>
